# Driver file version

Each `configs/*.json` file owns a top-level `"version"` (`major.minor.patch`). That value is the radio driver version HamBench shows for an installed radio. It is independent of `package.json` (the module zip) and of every other config in the module.

## When editing a driver

- Bump `"version"` in the same edit whenever that driver changes.
- A driver is the config plus every relative `$ref` it uses (schemas and memory maps).
- A shared schema change bumps every config that references it.
- Leave unchanged sibling configs, and their versions, untouched.
- Do not copy the module or `package.json` version onto configs.

From the radio module root, `node scripts/check-driver-versions.mjs` fails when a driver file changed without a higher version. CI runs it against the base revision.

## How to bump

| Change | Bump |
| --- | --- |
| New radio config | Start at `1.0.0` |
| Compatible addition (new optional CAT field, extra baud rate) | minor |
| Compatible fix (wrong expect byte, corrected skip range) | patch |
| Incompatible protocol or layout change | major |

A protocol fix bumps only that file. Sibling configs keep their own versions.
